I think that climate deniers exploit the  fact that we scientists talk a lot about  uncertainties deniers suggest that  uncertainty means untrue which is a  completely different way of how we  scientists think about uncertainties now  we know that we cannot predict future  climate science relies heavily on  modeling because we obviously cannot  change the climate deliberately and  conduct experiments the climate model is  a mathematical formulation of the  physical processes that play a role for  example fluid motion that is described  by the navier-stokes equations by the  way these equations are the same that  are used to optimize the flight behavior  of airplanes because they demonstrate  the flow around the airfoil we all are  easy to use airplanes that have been  optimized by these equations and by  models we don't think that uncertainty  in that respect equals untrue now once  we have this model we can use that model  in order to conduct experiments like in  a virtual laboratory we can for example  change the assumptions on for example  co2 emissions and see how the climate  system reacts we are able to not only  say how future scenarios change the  climate system but we can even say how  reliable these results are that is why  in the currently released IPCC reports  you can find words like it is likely  very likely or almost certain when we  talk about future climate projections  deniers are skeptics often understand  uncertainty as being not true we  understand uncertainty as being not  completely under our control that means  we have some variability in the data for  example that we need to account for  coming back to your question why do  climate deniers ignore  facts I don't know that I think some do  it because there's always an alternative  opinion in science some do it because  they have massive political or financial  interests in denying the facts some of  them because they simply don't know  better I hope that with these  explanations I could explain the facts a  little bit better and so if you use an  airplane that was optimized by a model  then you can also trust the simulations  and the methods that are behind climate  modeling
 

